byid['1975-380.2']['reconstruction']+=r' \ours\ The cusp obstruction is elementary: \(t\) is integral over \(\mathbb C[t^2,t^3]\), since it satisfies \(T^2-t^2=0\), but it does not lie in that ring. Thus the ring is not normal, whereas the coordinate ring of a smooth affine curve is normal.'
